<exercisegroup xml:id="exercisegroup-vectors-parallel">
<title>Recognizing parallel vectors</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	determine whether the two vectors are parallel.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-3,4) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-12,16) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> Yes, <m>\uvec{v} = 4 \uvec{u} </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (5,-8) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (10,-17) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> No. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (18,-6) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-12,4) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> Yes, <m>\uvec{u} = -\frac{3}{2} \uvec{v} </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (-6,3,-1) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (-2,1,-1/3) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> Yes, <m>\uvec{u} = 3 \uvec{v} </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (20,-5,10) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (32,-8,16) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> Yes, <m>\uvec{v} = \frac{8}{5} \uvec{u} </m>. </p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p> <m> \uvec{u} = (7,2,-9) </m>, <m> \uvec{v} = (14,6,-1) </m> </p></statement>

	<answer><p> No. </p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
